    "details": "MIME-tools project reports:\n\n> Many security issues were addressed (see the following ten CVEs)\n> Issues were brought to my attention, and patches supplied, by the\n> CPANSec security group.\n>\n> - CVE-2026-116264 invalid parameter hides boundary/filename\n> - CVE-2026-116265 RFC 2231 boundary skips ambiguity checks\n> - CVE-2026-116266 boundary changed by decoding not flagged\n> - CVE-2026-116267 indent stored per message per level\n> - CVE-2026-116268 unclosed \\\"(\\\" comments backtrack CPU exhaustion\n> - CVE-2026-116269 RFC 2231 language tag empties filename\n> - CVE-2026-116270 each bad \\\"=?\\\" copies the input into \\$@\n> - CVE-2026-116271 FileUnder reuses a pre-created directory\n> - CVE-2026-116272 comment hides a duplicate boundary\n> - CVE-2026-116273 max_parts and max_depth unlimited\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0557",
